 ## Overview
-Computes the exact signed distance from a point to a regular octahedron centered at the origin with size parameter $s$ [S1, unofficial]. It solves the primitive definition problem for ray marching by providing a closed-form analytic solution, avoiding iterative approximation. It is distinguished from its siblings, the [Hexagonal Prism](2348-hexagonal-prism.md) and [Triangular Prism](2865-triangular-prism.md), by its specific symmetry group and face geometry, offering a distinct aesthetic for procedural geometry [S1, unofficial].
